# Code owners for microsoft/azcapman.
#
# GitHub requests a review from these owners whenever a pull request touches a
# matching path:
# https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/managing-your-repositorys-settings-and-features/customizing-your-repository/about-code-owners
#
# Why these paths: AGENTS.md rule 1.4 treats the checked-in supply chain checks as
# tripwires rather than enforcement, because a pull request can weaken a checker and
# the workflow it guards in the same diff. GitHub recommends code owners on workflow
# files for that reason:
# https://docs.github.com/en/actions/reference/security/secure-use#using-codeowners-to-monitor-changes
#
# What this does and doesn't do here. "Require review from Code Owners" is off on the
# default branch, so this notifies rather than blocks. GitHub doesn't request a review
# from the author of a pull request, so on a pull request opened by the maintainer
# below it does nothing at all. Its effect is to notify that maintainer when anyone
# else proposes a change to CI, to the constitution, or to what ships as a plugin.
# The required status checks and the pinned-SHA actions policy are what enforce
# rule 1.4.

# CI definitions, the scripts CI executes, and the plugin manifests under .github.
/.github/ @MSBrett

# The repository constitution, including the supply chain rules in section 1.4.
/AGENTS.md @MSBrett

# Manifests and the agent file that determine what ships to anyone installing this
# repository as a plugin.
/.claude-plugin/ @MSBrett
/.codex-plugin/ @MSBrett
/agents/ @MSBrett
